      'ONLY YAHWEH CAN JUDGE ME — study what He judges, and walk in the winning hand. Darrell spoke this lesson into the app. It is a big lesson with many small parts. ONLY YAHWEH JUDGES. A singer named Tupac had a song called Only God Can Judge Me. Darrell says that is true. The Bible says, "There is one lawgiver, who is able to save and to destroy" (James 4:12). Yahweh is the one true Judge. But Darrell asks a good question. If Yahweh is the Judge, what will He judge? We should find out! The Bible says "every one of us shall give account of himself to God" (Romans 14:12). That means each of us will tell Him what we did. So we study His Word. The Bible says, "Study to shew thyself approved unto God" (2 Timothy 2:15). When we know what He wants, and we are at peace with Him through Jesus, life gets beautiful. BRAG ON HIM. Some kids brag about how fast they run. Some brag about their toys. The Bible says, "He that glorieth, let him glory in the Lord" (1 Corinthians 1:31). That means if you want to brag, brag about Yahweh! Darrell says any other bragging looks silly next to forever. HARD AND GOOD. Darrell says life is hard and beautiful at the same time. He has had hard days. But he has had fun the whole way! The Bible says, "the joy of the LORD is your strength" (Nehemiah 8:10). Joy makes you strong. The Bible also says, "He hath made every thing beautiful in his time" (Ecclesiastes 3:11). Darrell says there are many good people in the world. And some people who were not good become good. The Bible says, "such were some of you: but ye are washed" (1 Corinthians 6:11). Jesus can make anyone new. PEOPLE MATTER MOST. Darrell says computers and AI are fine. But nothing is better than real friends. Talk to people. Sit with them. Listen to them. You learn so much! No money is better than a good friend. When you talk with a friend, you see things a new way. You learn how they think. You grow. A screen cannot hug you. A screen cannot sit with you when you are sad. The Bible says, "It is not good that the man should be alone" (Genesis 2:18). And it says, "Iron sharpeneth iron" (Proverbs 27:17). Good friends make each other better. NOT REALLY ENEMIES. Jesus said, "Love your enemies" (Matthew 5:44). That is hard! But Darrell says they are not really enemies. Maybe something sad happened in their home when they were little. Something happened in your home too. Think about what happened in theirs. The Bible says, "we wrestle not against flesh and blood" (Ephesians 6:12). That means our fight is not with people. So the next time a kid is mean to you, stop and think. Maybe they had a hard day at home. Maybe no one is kind to them. You can pray for them. You can still be kind. On the cross, Jesus prayed, "Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do" (Luke 23:34). ONE TEAM. Darrell says grown-ups sometimes get mad at each other about who should lead the country. But he believes they agree on most things. He hopes we can do the good things we all agree on. Jesus said, "if a house be divided against itself, that house cannot stand" (Mark 3:25). A team that fights itself cannot win. The Bible says, "how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity" (Psalms 133:1). Unity means being one team. THE KING CAME DOWN. Jesus is the King. He left His throne in heaven and came down to us. The Bible says He "took upon him the form of a servant" (Philippians 2:7). The Bible also says, "He came unto his own, and his own received him not" (John 1:11). Darrell says the leaders who knew the Bible best were the ones who planned to hurt Him. That is sad. It tells us to know Jesus, not just know about Him. But the Bible says all of us needed the cross. It says, "All we like sheep have gone astray" (Isaiah 53:6). No one group did it. All of us needed Him. And Jesus said, "No man taketh it from me, but I lay it down of myself" (John 10:18). He chose to give His life because He loves us. WHO IS JESUS. Some people argue about what Jesus looked like. Darrell says that is not the big question. The big question is who He is! The Bible says Yahweh looks at the heart. Jesus asked His friends, "whom say ye that I am" (Matthew 16:15). Peter said, "Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God" (Matthew 16:16). Darrell believes that is true. That is why he loves his life! LEARN TO OWN. Darrell says it is good to learn how to own things, like a home. The Bible tells about a woman who "considereth a field, and buyeth it" (Proverbs 31:16). That means she thought hard and then bought land. Darrell says many of us were taught to work for others, but not how to own. So we must learn. Yahweh will teach us how. It is good to help others, and it is good to own things too. Everything really belongs to Yahweh, and we take care of it for Him. Darrell also says this. You can be the best one on a team and still get paid the least. That happened to him many times. The owners pick the pay. So learn to own, and one day you can help pick the pay too. SEVEN AND EIGHT. Darrell says to split your money into seven parts, or even eight. The Bible says, "Give a portion to seven, and also to eight" (Ecclesiastes 11:2). That way, if one part is lost, you still have the rest. You can try it with a jar or a box. Put a little in each part. Watch it grow! Darrell talks about houses. Buy one house. Then buy more. Let each house pay for itself. That takes a long time, and lots of care. LEARN A SKILL. Darrell says learning a skill can matter more than money right now. The Bible says, "with all thy getting get understanding" (Proverbs 4:7). A skill stays with you. FAMILY PICTURES. Darrell has old family pictures. Some show feathers and brown skin. His uncle knows that family story best, so Darrell lets his uncle tell it. Darrell talks about the Bible. THE WINNING HAND. Darrell says Yahweh’s law is the winning hand. It is like a game you cannot lose. The Bible calls it "the law of the Spirit of life in Christ Jesus" (Romans 8:2). Jesus paid for it with "the precious blood of Christ" (1 Peter 1:19). The Bible says, "for the joy that was set before him endured the cross" (Hebrews 12:2). He did it with joy, for us! WHAT WE CHECKED. Every Bible verse here comes from the King James Bible in this app. We checked that the song is really a Tupac song. We do not use any of its words. The stories about Darrell’s life are his own story. The two stories are made up to teach. SAY IT AGAIN. Only Yahweh judges, so learn what He wants. Brag on Him. Life is hard and good, and His joy makes you strong. People matter most. Love your enemies. Be one team. Jesus gave His life for all of us. Know who He is. Save in seven or eight parts. Learn a skill. Jesus gave us the winning hand. TALK ABOUT IT TOGETHER. Parents, ask your children who their best friend is and why, then listen to the end, and read Genesis 2:18 with them. Children, ask your mom, dad or grandparent what their home was like when they were little, and listen all the way through. Friends, tell one friend this week something you both like, and pray for each other. Do it once today, at the table, on the way, at bedtime, or first thing. So we all get healthy together, until we see that Yahweh has been right.',
